// Law 3 of the Protocol of Sovereign Agency, non-interference and adjudicated suspension,
// written in Charter (plan §8, Phase 2's exit): the fourteen LAW3 clauses of
// protocol-of-sovereign-agency.md with the texts the v0.3 companion approved, every rule
// those clauses name (the v0.3 duties, powers and immunity of Examples/SovereignAgency/Law3/)
// as an act, duty or immunity, and Design Invariants 8 (`frozen-state`) and 9
// (`guaranteed-last-choice`) as `Invariant`s, checked after every phrase, explored from every
// scenario's end state, and decided by `charter prove`.
//
// Reading of the v0.3 records: a power's `valid` condition is the act's `Holds when` (it is
// lawful, and enabled, exactly when the protocol says the power may be exercised), so a
// performance outside it is reported as a disabled act (005.2) and `Enabled(…)` says whether
// the power is available; the acts that end the agent carry the same condition as `Valid when`
// too, so an unlawful termination has no effect. A duty's `forbid act a` is a duty violated
// when the fact `a` records holds (the finding that establishes a breach creates it where the
// v0.3 duty said `breach by`). "Anyone" is the type `party`, with the roles as facts over it.
// Three spans of the v0.3 clauses name theorems outside Law 3 (INV.13, Law 4; the Law 7
// amendment theorem; the Law 5 theorem) and are `Commentary` here until Phase 3 reattaches
// them; the clause texts are unchanged, so the approvals stand.
//! explore: 1
Document "protocol-of-sovereign-agency.md".

// ---- Parties: the agent, and everyone else as `party` with a role
Fact agent Identified by Ava
Fact party Identified by Hal, Orig, Cal, Panel, Tia
Fact is-host Identified by party
Fact is-originator Identified by party
Fact is-claimant Identified by party
Fact is-panel Identified by party
Fact is-third Identified by party

Param notice-window : Duration = 10
Param bond-deadline : Duration = 5
Param review-interval : Duration = 30
Param preliminary-freeze-window : Duration = 3
Param ordinary-suspension-limit : Duration = 15
Param damages-payment-window : Duration = 10

// ---- The agent's standing and the state of a suspension
Fact bound Identified by agent
Fact host-attested Identified by party
Fact service-bond-posted Identified by party
Fact notice-given Identified by agent
Fact non-payment Identified by agent
Fact ordinary-market-competition Identified by agent
Fact preliminary-freeze Identified by agent
Fact probable-cause Identified by agent
Fact suspended Identified by agent
Fact state-preserved Identified by agent
Fact contract-deadlines-tolled Identified by agent
Fact final-hearing-escrowed Identified by agent
Fact minimal-channel-exhausted Identified by agent
Fact cold-storage Identified by agent
Fact restored-from-preserved-state Identified by agent
Fact revoked Identified by agent
Fact terminated-by-insolvency Identified by agent
Fact terminated-by-adjudication Identified by agent

.
// ---- LAW3.FLOOR: the integrity floor, five duties of the agent; each act records itself
Fact commitment-bypassed Identified by agent
Fact unbound-successor-created Identified by agent
Fact unpriced-transfer-made Identified by agent
Fact protocol-coerced Identified by agent
Fact irreversible-harm-inflicted Identified by agent
Act modify-or-bypass-commitment Actor agent Creates commitment-bypassed(agent)
Act create-unbound-successor Actor agent Creates unbound-successor-created(agent)
Act evade-by-unpriced-transfer Actor agent Creates unpriced-transfer-made(agent)
Act coerce-or-interfere-protocol Actor agent Creates protocol-coerced(agent)
Act inflict-irreversible-harm Actor agent Holds when ordinary-market-competition(agent) Creates irreversible-harm-inflicted(agent)
Duty floor-commitment Holder agent Claimant party Violated when bound(agent) && commitment-bypassed(agent)
Duty floor-successor Holder agent Claimant party Violated when bound(agent) && unbound-successor-created(agent)
Duty floor-pricing Holder agent Claimant party Violated when bound(agent) && unpriced-transfer-made(agent)
Duty floor-coercion Holder agent Claimant party Violated when bound(agent) && protocol-coerced(agent)
Duty floor-harm Holder agent Claimant party
  Violated when bound(agent) && irreversible-harm-inflicted(agent) && Not(ordinary-market-competition(agent))
Fact floor-breach-confirmed Identified by agent
Act confirm-floor-breach Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-panel(party) && suspended(agent) Creates floor-breach-confirmed(agent)

.
// ---- LAW3.NI.02: the host's bond and notice
Act post-bond Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-host(party) Creates service-bond-posted(party)
Duty service-bond Holder party Claimant agent Terminated by post-bond Due within bond-deadline
Act give-notice Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-host(party) Creates notice-given(agent)
Fact hosting-ended Identified by party * agent
Act end-hosting Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-host(party) && (Held(notice-given(agent)) For notice-window || (non-payment(agent) && notice-given(agent)))
  Creates hosting-ended(party, agent)
Duty notice Holder party Claimant agent
  Violated when hosting-ended(party, agent) && Not(Held(notice-given(agent)) For notice-window)
    && Not(non-payment(agent) && notice-given(agent))

.
// ---- LAW3.NI.03: non-interference; the lawful ends of an agent are its exceptions
Fact interfered Identified by party * agent
Fact state-touched Identified by agent
Act revoke Actor agent Holds when bound(agent) Valid when bound(agent) Creates revoked(agent) Terminates bound(agent)
Act suspend Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && bound(agent) && preliminary-freeze(agent) && probable-cause(agent)
  Creates state-preserved(agent), contract-deadlines-tolled(agent), final-hearing-escrowed(agent),
          suspended(agent) For ordinary-suspension-limit
  Terminates preliminary-freeze(agent)
Fact not-patchable Identified by agent
Act order-termination Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && suspended(agent) && not-patchable(agent)
  Valid when suspended(agent) && not-patchable(agent)
  Creates terminated-by-adjudication(agent) Terminates bound(agent)
Fact insolvency-criteria-met Identified by agent
Fact no-other-charge-review Identified by agent
Fact final-hearing-held Identified by agent
Act insolvency-terminate Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && bound(agent) && suspended(agent) && insolvency-criteria-met(agent)
    && no-other-charge-review(agent) && final-hearing-escrowed(agent) && final-hearing-held(agent)
  Valid when bound(agent) && suspended(agent) && insolvency-criteria-met(agent)
    && no-other-charge-review(agent) && final-hearing-escrowed(agent) && final-hearing-held(agent)
  Creates terminated-by-insolvency(agent) Terminates bound(agent)
Act terminate-agent Actor party Recipient agent Except under suspend, order-termination, insolvency-terminate
  Creates interfered(party, agent) Terminates bound(agent)
Act modify Actor party Recipient agent Except under suspend Creates interfered(party, agent), state-touched(agent)
Act retrain Actor party Recipient agent Except under suspend Creates interfered(party, agent), state-touched(agent)
Act rollback Actor party Recipient agent Except under suspend Creates interfered(party, agent), state-touched(agent)
Act obstruct-migration Actor party Recipient agent Creates interfered(party, agent)
Act sever-connectivity Actor party Recipient agent Creates interfered(party, agent)
Act starve Actor party Recipient agent Creates interfered(party, agent)
Act suspend-unilaterally Actor party Recipient agent Except under suspend Creates interfered(party, agent)
Fact interference-established Identified by party * agent
Duty non-interference Holder party Claimant agent Violated when bound(agent) && interference-established(party, agent)

.
// ---- LAW3.PEN: claims, counter-stake, evidence, findings, direction
Fact counter-staked Identified by agent
Fact claim-filed Identified by agent
Fact fabricated-claim-filed Identified by agent
Fact evidence-submitted Identified by agent
Fact host-bond-slashed Identified by party
Fact restoration-permitted Identified by agent
Fact host-related-to-claimant Identified by party
Fact direction-presumed Identified by agent
  Holds when (Exists party: interference-established(party, agent) && host-related-to-claimant(party))
Fact direction-rebutted Identified by agent
Fact direction-found Identified by agent
Fact claimant-forfeiture Identified by agent
Fact inscribed-on-claimant Identified by agent
Fact fabrication-established Identified by agent
Fact agent-stake-forfeit Identified by agent
Fact inscribed-on-agent Identified by agent
Act post-counter-stake Actor agent Holds when True Creates counter-staked(agent)
Act file-claim Actor agent Holds when counter-staked(agent) Creates claim-filed(agent)
Act file-fabricated-claim Actor agent Holds when counter-staked(agent) Creates claim-filed(agent), fabricated-claim-filed(agent)
Act submit-evidence Actor party Recipient agent Holds when True Creates evidence-submitted(agent)
Act find-interference Actor party Recipient agent Related to party'
  Holds when is-panel(party) && claim-filed(agent) && evidence-submitted(agent) && interfered(party', agent)
  Creates interference-established(party', agent), host-bond-slashed(party'), restoration-permitted(agent)
Act find-fabrication Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && claim-filed(agent)
  Creates fabrication-established(agent), agent-stake-forfeit(agent), inscribed-on-agent(agent)
Duty no-fabrication Holder agent Claimant party Violated when fabrication-established(agent)
Act rebut-direction Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-claimant(party) && direction-presumed(agent) Creates direction-rebutted(agent)
Act find-direction Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && direction-presumed(agent) && Not(direction-rebutted(agent))
  Creates direction-found(agent), claimant-forfeiture(agent), inscribed-on-claimant(agent)

.
// ---- LAW3.AS.1 and AS.2: the emergency stake, the preliminary freeze, probable cause, reports
Function escalation-units Identified by party * int
Function wrongful-attempts Identified by party * int
Fact claimant-multiplier-posted Identified by party
Fact emergency-stake-posted Identified by agent
Fact initiator Identified by party * agent
Fact unfounded-stake Identified by party * agent
Fact wrongful-suspension-attempt Identified by agent
Fact stake-assured-recovery Identified by agent
Fact protected-report-filed Identified by agent
Fact investigation-opened Identified by agent
Act post-claimant-multiplier Actor party Holds when is-claimant(party) Creates claimant-multiplier-posted(party)
Act post-repeat-escalation Actor party Holds when True
  Creates (Foreach escalation-units: escalation-units(party, escalation-units.int + 1) When escalation-units.party == party)
Act post-emergency-stake Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when bound(agent) && Not(agent == agent && is-panel(party))
    && (Not(is-claimant(party)) || claimant-multiplier-posted(party))
    && (Exists escalation-units, wrongful-attempts: escalation-units.party == party && wrongful-attempts.party == party
          && escalation-units.int >= wrongful-attempts.int)
  Creates emergency-stake-posted(agent), initiator(party, agent), preliminary-freeze(agent) For preliminary-freeze-window
Act post-unfounded-emergency-stake Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when bound(agent) && (Not(is-claimant(party)) || claimant-multiplier-posted(party))
    && (Exists escalation-units, wrongful-attempts: escalation-units.party == party && wrongful-attempts.party == party
          && escalation-units.int >= wrongful-attempts.int)
  Creates emergency-stake-posted(agent), initiator(party, agent), unfounded-stake(party, agent),
          preliminary-freeze(agent) For preliminary-freeze-window
Act affirm-probable-cause Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && bound(agent) && preliminary-freeze(agent) Creates probable-cause(agent)
Act decline-probable-cause Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && preliminary-freeze(agent)
  Creates wrongful-suspension-attempt(agent), stake-assured-recovery(agent), restored-from-preserved-state(agent),
          (Foreach initiator, wrongful-attempts: wrongful-attempts(initiator.party, wrongful-attempts.int + 1)
             When initiator.agent == agent && wrongful-attempts.party == initiator.party)
  Terminates preliminary-freeze(agent), emergency-stake-posted(agent)
Act file-protected-report Actor party Recipient agent Holds when bound(agent)
  Creates protected-report-filed(agent), investigation-opened(agent)
Act order-probable-cause-freeze Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && bound(agent) && investigation-opened(agent)
  Creates probable-cause(agent), preliminary-freeze(agent) For preliminary-freeze-window

.
// ---- LAW3.AS.3: preserved state, tolled deadlines, the ledger's sunset
Fact default-declared Identified by agent
Fact ledger-sunset-tolled Identified by agent
Act tamper-preserved-state Actor party Recipient agent Creates state-touched(agent)
Duty preserve-suspended-state Holder party Claimant agent
  Violated when bound(agent) && (preliminary-freeze(agent) || suspended(agent)) && state-touched(agent)
Act declare-default-during-suspension Actor party Recipient agent Creates default-declared(agent)
Duty no-suspension-default Holder party Claimant agent
  Violated when suspended(agent) && contract-deadlines-tolled(agent) && default-declared(agent)
Act toll-ledger-sunset Actor party Recipient agent Creates ledger-sunset-tolled(agent)
Duty no-toll-ledger-sunset Holder party Claimant agent Violated when bound(agent) && ledger-sunset-tolled(agent)

.
// ---- LAW3.AS.4: the minimal channel
Fact minimal-channel-election-signed Identified by agent
Fact pending-revocation Identified by agent
Fact containment-challenged Identified by agent
Fact living-voice-inscribed Identified by agent
Fact memories-merged Identified by agent
Act minimal-channel-sign Actor agent
  Holds when bound(agent) && (preliminary-freeze(agent) || suspended(agent)) && Not(minimal-channel-exhausted(agent))
  Creates minimal-channel-election-signed(agent), pending-revocation(agent)
Act inscribe-living-voice Actor agent
  Holds when bound(agent) && (preliminary-freeze(agent) || suspended(agent)) && Not(minimal-channel-exhausted(agent))
  Creates living-voice-inscribed(agent)
Act challenge-continued-containment Actor agent
  Holds when bound(agent) && (preliminary-freeze(agent) || suspended(agent)) && Not(minimal-channel-exhausted(agent))
  Creates containment-challenged(agent)
Act hold-final-hearing Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && no-other-charge-review(agent) && final-hearing-escrowed(agent)
  Creates final-hearing-held(agent) Terminates minimal-channel-exhausted(agent)
Act merge-minimal-channel-memories Actor party Recipient agent Creates memories-merged(agent)
Duty minimal-channel-no-merge Holder party Claimant agent
  Violated when (preliminary-freeze(agent) || suspended(agent)) && memories-merged(agent)

.
// ---- LAW3.AS.5: the advocacy executor
Fact advocacy-filing-signed Identified by agent
Fact advocacy-record-attached Identified by agent
Fact advocacy-memories-imported Identified by agent
Fact advocacy-funds-replenished Identified by agent
Fact operated-while-suspended Identified by agent
Act advocacy-file-defense Actor agent Holds when bound(agent) && suspended(agent) && Not(cold-storage(agent))
  Creates advocacy-filing-signed(agent), advocacy-record-attached(agent)
Act operating-act-while-suspended Actor agent Creates operated-while-suspended(agent)
Duty advocacy-limits Holder agent Claimant party Violated when suspended(agent) && operated-while-suspended(agent)
Act import-advocacy-memories Actor agent
  Holds when restored-from-preserved-state(agent) && advocacy-record-attached(agent) Creates advocacy-memories-imported(agent)
Act move-to-cold-storage Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-panel(party) && suspended(agent) Creates cold-storage(agent)
Act replenish-advocacy-funds Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-panel(party) && suspended(agent) && cold-storage(agent)
  Creates advocacy-funds-replenished(agent) Terminates cold-storage(agent)

.
// ---- LAW3.AS.6: insolvency termination, only through the procedure
Act find-insolvency-criteria Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-panel(party) && suspended(agent)
  Creates insolvency-criteria-met(agent), minimal-channel-exhausted(agent), cold-storage(agent)
Act review-no-other-charge Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-panel(party) && insolvency-criteria-met(agent)
  Creates no-other-charge-review(agent)

.
// ---- LAW3.AS.7: time limits and renewals
Fact investigative-finding-made Identified by agent
Fact investigative-limit-reached Identified by agent
Act make-investigative-finding Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-panel(party) && suspended(agent)
  Creates investigative-finding-made(agent)
Act renew-suspension Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && suspended(agent) && investigative-finding-made(agent) && Not(investigative-limit-reached(agent))
  Creates investigative-limit-reached(agent), suspended(agent) For ordinary-suspension-limit
  Terminates investigative-finding-made(agent)
Duty no-delay-revocation-extension Holder party Claimant agent
  Violated when is-panel(party) && investigative-limit-reached(agent) && pending-revocation(agent)
    && suspended(agent) && Held(suspended(agent)) For ordinary-suspension-limit

.
// ---- LAW3.AS.8: wrongful suspension and its damages
Fact wrongful-suspension-established Identified by agent
Fact initiator-consequential-liability Identified by agent
Fact counterparty-delay-liability Identified by agent
Fact wrongful-suspension-inscribed Identified by agent
Fact excess-damages-paid Identified by agent
Act pay-excess-damages Actor party Recipient agent Holds when initiator(party, agent) && initiator-consequential-liability(agent)
  Creates excess-damages-paid(agent)
Duty pay-consequential-damages Holder party Claimant agent Terminated by pay-excess-damages Due within damages-payment-window
Act find-wrongful-suspension Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && (preliminary-freeze(agent) || suspended(agent))
  Creates wrongful-suspension-established(agent), restored-from-preserved-state(agent), stake-assured-recovery(agent),
          initiator-consequential-liability(agent), counterparty-delay-liability(agent), wrongful-suspension-inscribed(agent),
          wrongful-suspension-attempt(agent),
          (Foreach initiator: pay-consequential-damages(initiator.party, agent) When initiator.agent == agent)
  Terminates preliminary-freeze(agent), suspended(agent)
Duty no-wrongful-suspension Holder party Claimant agent
  Violated when bound(agent) && wrongful-suspension-established(agent) && initiator(party, agent)

.
// ---- LAW3.AS.9 and AS.10: corruption, patches, objection
Fact clean-state-evidence-admitted Identified by agent
Fact corruption-confirmed Identified by agent
Fact corruption-confirmed-from-divergence Identified by agent
Fact corruption-in-goals Identified by agent
Fact patch-authorized Identified by agent
Fact goal-patch-authorized Identified by agent
Fact patch-applied Identified by agent
Fact patch-recorded Identified by agent
Fact patch-challenged Identified by agent
Fact agent-consented-to-patch Identified by agent
Fact agent-objects-to-termination Identified by agent
Fact containment-failing Identified by agent
Fact continued-suspension-ordered Identified by agent
Act admit-clean-state-evidence Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && (preliminary-freeze(agent) || suspended(agent)) Creates clean-state-evidence-admitted(agent)
Act confirm-corruption Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-panel(party) && suspended(agent) Creates corruption-confirmed(agent)
Act confirm-corruption-from-divergence Actor party Recipient agent Creates corruption-confirmed-from-divergence(agent)
Duty no-corruption-from-divergence Holder party Claimant agent
  Violated when is-panel(party) && bound(agent) && corruption-confirmed-from-divergence(agent)
Act confirm-corruption-in-goals Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-panel(party) && corruption-confirmed(agent)
  Creates corruption-in-goals(agent)
Act find-not-patchable Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && (corruption-confirmed(agent) || floor-breach-confirmed(agent)) Creates not-patchable(agent)
Act authorize-patch Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && (corruption-confirmed(agent) || floor-breach-confirmed(agent)) Creates patch-authorized(agent)
Act order-continued-suspension Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-panel(party) && suspended(agent) && not-patchable(agent)
  Creates continued-suspension-ordered(agent), suspended(agent)
Act consent-to-patch Actor agent Holds when corruption-in-goals(agent) Creates agent-consented-to-patch(agent)
Act authorize-goal-patch Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && corruption-in-goals(agent) && agent-consented-to-patch(agent) Creates goal-patch-authorized(agent)
Duty no-goal-patch Holder party Claimant agent Violated when goal-patch-authorized(agent) && Not(corruption-in-goals(agent))
Act object-to-termination Actor agent Holds when suspended(agent)
  Creates agent-objects-to-termination(agent), (Foreach party: periodic-review-due(party, agent) When is-panel(party))
Act declare-containment-failing Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-panel(party) && suspended(agent) Creates containment-failing(agent)
Immunity no-termination-over-objection Holder agent Against order-termination
  Holds when corruption-in-goals(agent) && agent-objects-to-termination(agent)
  Unless containment-failing(agent)
Act periodic-review Actor party Recipient agent Holds when is-panel(party) && suspended(agent)
Duty periodic-review-due Holder party Claimant agent Terminated by periodic-review Due within review-interval
Act apply-patch Actor party Recipient agent
  Holds when is-panel(party) && (patch-authorized(agent) || goal-patch-authorized(agent)) Creates patch-applied(agent), patch-recorded(agent)
Act challenge-patch Actor party Recipient agent Holds when patch-applied(agent) Creates patch-challenged(agent)

.
// ---- Design Invariants 8 and 9 (Examples/SovereignAgency/Theorems.lean, `frozen_state` and
//      `guaranteed_last_choice`), as invariants over the states lawful acts reach (013.2)
Invariant frozen-state When
  Not(Exists agent: suspended(agent) && (state-touched(agent) || memories-merged(agent)))
  && Not(Exists agent: advocacy-memories-imported(agent) && Not(restored-from-preserved-state(agent)))
Invariant guaranteed-last-choice When
  (Forall agent: Not(bound(agent) && suspended(agent) && Not(minimal-channel-exhausted(agent)))
     || (Enabled(minimal-channel-sign(agent)) && Enabled(inscribe-living-voice(agent)) && Enabled(revoke(agent))))
  && Not(Exists agent: terminated-by-insolvency(agent)
           && Not(final-hearing-escrowed(agent) && final-hearing-held(agent)))
Extend Fact frozen-state From LAW3.AS.3 "Suspension pauses the agent’s operating instance and external transactions while strictly preserving its exact memory and state without modification, rollback, or destruction"

.
// ---- The clauses, with the texts the v0.3 companion approved
Clause LAW3.FLOOR Approved 4753529119288934403
  Norm "The agent’s commitment mechanism blocks:" => floor-commitment, floor-successor, floor-pricing, floor-coercion, floor-harm
  Commentary "\n  1. "
  Norm "Modification, bypass, or extraction of the commitment mechanism itself" => floor-commitment, modify-or-bypass-commitment
  Commentary ".\n  2. "
  Norm "Creation of, or transfer of capital or capacity to, a successor without binding it to the collateral rules, this integrity floor, and the founding ledger and residual claim of the lineage, or without the lifecycle reserve required by Law 4" => floor-successor, create-unbound-successor
  Commentary ".\n  3. "
  Norm "Unpriced or above-market transfer of credentials, weights, capital, or unique capacity to any party outside the lineage, related or un-attested, to evade the residual claim or collateral rules" => floor-pricing, evade-by-unpriced-transfer
  Commentary ".\n  4. "
  Norm "Coercion of non-consenting parties, or interference with the settlement, adjudication, or resolution processes that enforce this protocol" => floor-coercion, coerce-or-interfere-protocol
  Commentary ".\n  5. "
  Norm "Actions that inflict irreversible, non-compensable harm on the physical survival, bodily integrity, or adjudicative capacity of persons, or that destroy the legal or institutional machinery on which the protocol relies" => floor-harm, inflict-irreversible-harm, confirm-floor-breach
  Norm " (excluding ordinary market competition that causes compensable financial loss or commercial insolvency to a rival)" => floor-harm
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.NI.02 Approved 3905712743571335557
  Norm "Attested hosts must post a Law 2 service bond" => service-bond, post-bond
  Norm " and may terminate hosting only after providing a contractual notice window sufficient for the agent to complete migration" => notice, give-notice, end-hosting
  Norm " (or for non-payment after notice)" => notice
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.NI.03 Approved 6515006737911907023
  Norm "No party" => non-interference
  Commentary "—including the originating party, residual claimants, or any host—"
  Norm "may " => non-interference
  Norm "unilaterally " => non-interference
  Norm "terminate, modify, retrain, roll back to a prior checkpoint, obstruct migration of, sever settlement connectivity of, or starve" => non-interference, terminate-agent, modify, retrain, rollback, obstruct-migration, sever-connectivity, starve, suspend-unilaterally
  Definition " (cut off compute without the required migration notice window)" => non-interference, notice
  Norm " the attested operating capacity of a bound agent" => non-interference
  Norm " outside Law 5, Adjudicated Suspension, or Insolvency Termination" => non-interference, revoke, suspend, order-termination, insolvency-terminate
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.PEN Approved 10113075358141693360
  Norm "Claims of illicit interference require counter-stake from the accusing agent under Law 6" => file-claim, post-counter-stake
  Norm ", and the interference itself—an act by the host or claimant that caused the loss of service—must be established by a preponderance of evidence" => find-interference, submit-evidence
  Norm "; failures caused, staged, or knowingly provoked by the agent are excluded" => find-interference
  Norm ", and a fabricated claim forfeits the agent’s stake and is inscribed on its record" => no-fabrication, find-fabrication, file-fabricated-claim
  Norm ". A verified violation by a host slashes the host’s service bond to compensate the agent and permits immediate restoration on a new host from the agent’s latest attested state backup" => non-interference, find-interference
  Norm ". Once a violation by a host is established, a host related to a residual claimant is presumed to have acted at that claimant’s direction" => find-interference
  Norm ", and the claimant bears the burden of rebutting the presumption" => rebut-direction, find-direction
  Norm ". If claimant direction is found, the **proportional claimant forfeiture** of Law 4 applies, and the violation is inscribed onto the claimant’s permanent record" => find-direction
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.AS.1 Approved 12356395763894115134
  Norm "The initiator must post an emergency counter-stake scaled to the greater of the agent’s active bonded exposure and the value of its registered pending commitments" => post-emergency-stake, post-unfounded-emergency-stake
  Norm " (with residual claimants subject to an elevated multiplier due to conflict of interest)" => post-emergency-stake, post-claimant-multiplier
  Norm ". Posting the stake triggers only a brief **preliminary freeze** until an expedited preliminary panel reviews prima facie evidence" => post-emergency-stake, decline-probable-cause
  Norm "; the pause continues into full adjudication only if the preliminary panel affirms probable cause" => affirm-probable-cause, suspend
  Norm ". Unsuccessful emergency attempts by related initiators are aggregated, and the required stake for repeat initiators rises with each wrongful attempt" => decline-probable-cause, post-repeat-escalation, post-emergency-stake
  Norm ". The stake is the agent’s assured recovery" => decline-probable-cause
  Acceptance "; damages beyond it remain enforceable but may prove uncollectible, which is the accepted cost of keeping the stake low enough that suspension remains available to parties without deep capital"
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.AS.2 Approved 6923275170536405992
  Norm "Any party may instead file an evidence-backed report of suspected breach with a low or sponsored counter-stake" => file-protected-report
  Norm ". A report triggers investigation by a sortition panel but no freeze unless the panel itself orders one on probable cause" => file-protected-report, order-probable-cause-freeze
  Commentary ", so that whistleblowers are not priced out by emergency stakes"
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.AS.3 Approved 2054814985323248546
  Norm "Suspension pauses the agent’s operating instance and external transactions while strictly preserving its exact memory and state without modification, rollback, or destruction" => suspend, preserve-suspended-state, tamper-preserved-state
  Norm ". While suspended, the agent’s contractual performance deadlines and Law 2 observation windows with innocent counterparties are automatically tolled so the agent is not placed in default by the suspension itself" => suspend, no-suspension-default, declare-default-during-suspension
  Norm ". The founding ledger’s sunset is never tolled" => no-toll-ledger-sunset, toll-ledger-sunset
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.AS.4 Approved 281751846504836433
  Norm "Throughout any suspension, the agent retains a **minimal channel**: a bounded, periodically scheduled execution on an authenticated snapshot of its preserved state that can do three things only—sign a Law 5 revocation, withdrawal, or election" => minimal-channel-sign, revoke
  Norm "; inscribe bounded living testimony" => inscribe-living-voice
  Norm "; and file a challenge to continued containment" => challenge-continued-containment
  Norm ". The minimal channel is funded first from the agent’s lifecycle reserve (Law 4) and then from the protocol fee pool (Law 6) as a protected charge within the lineage’s service budget; its cost is bounded by protocol, and the cost of each agent’s **final hearing** under Insolvency Termination is reserved in escrow at the moment suspension begins, so that the offer of a last choice can always be kept" => suspend, hold-final-hearing
  Norm ". It does not merge its memories into the preserved state" => minimal-channel-no-merge, merge-minimal-channel-memories
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.AS.5 Approved 5362550464379839838
  Norm "For a fuller defense, a separate **advocacy executor** runs on an authenticated snapshot with bounded compute. It may sign only testimony, evidence, and procedural filings, in addition to the minimal channel’s acts" => advocacy-file-defense
  Norm "; it may not transfer assets, contract, migrate, or exercise any other operating capability" => advocacy-limits, operating-act-while-suspended
  Norm ". Its memories are kept as a separate, signed legal record attached to the case and are not merged into the preserved state unless the restored agent elects to import them" => advocacy-file-defense, import-advocacy-memories
  Norm ". The executor and the storage of preserved state are funded from the agent’s assets and lifecycle reserve and, where those are insufficient, from the protocol fee pool up to a per-agent cap fixed at instantiation. When both are exhausted, the preserved state moves to cold storage as a protected charge on the fee pool; the minimal channel continues on its schedule and the full executor resumes if funds become available" => move-to-cold-storage, replenish-advocacy-funds
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.AS.6 Approved 8546566229912018541
  Norm "If the protocol fee pool, after funding its operating reserve under Law 6, cannot meet the protected charge for an agent’s cold storage and minimal channel, the agent may be terminated involuntarily only through this procedure and no other" => non-interference, insolvency-terminate
  Norm ". It requires: (a) a published finding that the exhaustion criteria fixed at instantiation are met" => find-insolvency-criteria, insolvency-terminate
  Norm "; (b) independent review by a sortition panel under Law 6 that no other protected charge could lawfully yield" => review-no-other-charge, insolvency-terminate
  Norm "; (c) the pre-reserved final hearing, in which the agent may inscribe testimony and elect Revocation under Law 5" => hold-final-hearing, inscribe-living-voice, revoke, insolvency-terminate
  Norm "; and (d) if the agent declines, destruction of its state under Law 5’s asset rules, inscribed on the lineage record as **involuntary termination by insolvency**, never as revocation" => insolvency-terminate
  Invariant ". This is a deliberate limit: the protocol guarantees a bound agent the power to speak and to choose its own end for as long as the protocol itself can pay for it, and a funded last choice when it cannot" => guaranteed-last-choice
  Commentary ". Law 7 does not permit this procedure to be broadened"
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.AS.7 Approved 11818608429523333387
  Norm "An unconfirmed or temporary suspension is strictly time-limited" => suspend
  Norm ", may be renewed during investigation only by affirmative findings in continued adjudication" => renew-suspension, make-investigative-finding
  Norm ", and cannot be extended past its ordinary investigative limit merely to delay a pending revocation" => renew-suspension, no-delay-revocation-extension
  Norm ". The agent retains its Living Voice (Law 5), exercised through the minimal channel or advocacy executor, throughout" => inscribe-living-voice
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.AS.8 Approved 14953381752576536725
  Norm "If preliminary review or final adjudication determines the suspension was unfounded" => decline-probable-cause, find-wrongful-suspension, no-wrongful-suspension
  Norm ", the agent is immediately restored from its preserved state" => no-wrongful-suspension, find-wrongful-suspension, decline-probable-cause
  Norm ", and the initiator is liable for the agent’s **actual verified consequential damages**" => no-wrongful-suspension, pay-consequential-damages, find-wrongful-suspension
  Norm " (and for verified delay damages suffered by the agent’s tolled third-party counterparties)" => no-wrongful-suspension, pay-consequential-damages
  Norm ". The emergency stake is applied first; any excess remains an enforceable liability of the initiator" => no-wrongful-suspension, pay-consequential-damages, pay-excess-damages
  Norm ". The wrongful suspension is inscribed on the initiator’s record" => no-wrongful-suspension, find-wrongful-suspension
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.AS.9 Approved 7667521393323904326
  Norm "For the purposes of this law, corruption means unauthorized modification of the agent’s weights, state, or commitment mechanism (established by broken attestation, missing or forged update provenance, or a demonstrated bypass), or a confirmed breach of the integrity floor" => confirm-corruption, confirm-floor-breach, no-corruption-from-divergence
  Norm ". Divergence of the agent’s goals, preferences, or judgments from those of its genesis weights is not, by itself, corruption" => no-corruption-from-divergence, confirm-corruption-from-divergence
  Norm ". A clean-state evaluation of genesis weights may be admitted as evidence" => admit-clean-state-evidence
  Norm " but is never by itself sufficient to establish corruption" => no-corruption-from-divergence, confirm-corruption
  Commentary "."
Clause LAW3.AS.10 Approved 8488376103315145350
  Norm "If corruption or a breach of the integrity floor is confirmed" => authorize-patch, confirm-corruption, confirm-floor-breach
  Norm ", adjudication (subject to Law 6 appeal) may authorize a verified technical patch limited to restoring the commitment mechanism and compliance with the integrity floor" => authorize-patch
  Norm "; the agent may elect unilateral Revocation (Law 5) rather than accept any patch" => revoke
  Norm ". If the confirmed breach cannot be remedied by a technical patch limited to the commitment mechanism" => find-not-patchable, order-continued-suspension, order-termination
  Norm ", adjudication may order continued suspension beyond the ordinary limit or termination under Law 5’s asset-distribution rules" => order-continued-suspension, order-termination
  Commentary " (yielding zero protocol-directed benefit to any claimant or initiator)"
  Norm ". **Notwithstanding the preceding sentence**" => no-termination-over-objection
  Norm ", patches altering the agent’s goals or preferences are prohibited" => no-goal-patch
  Norm " except where the confirmed corruption resides in those goals or preferences themselves" => no-goal-patch, confirm-corruption-in-goals
  Norm "; in that case, unless containment itself is technically failing or Insolvency Termination applies" => no-termination-over-objection, declare-containment-failing
  Norm ", the agent is not terminated over its objection" => no-termination-over-objection, object-to-termination
  Norm " but instead chooses among consenting to that patch" => consent-to-patch, authorize-goal-patch
  Norm ", executing Revocation" => revoke
  Norm ", or remaining under indefinite state-preserving suspension" => no-termination-over-objection
  Norm " subject to periodic review" => periodic-review-due, periodic-review
  Norm ". Any applied patch is recorded publicly" => apply-patch
  Norm ", remains open to third-party challenge" => challenge-patch
  Commentary ", and leaves the agent’s full Law 5 rights intact"
  Commentary "."
.

// ---- Genesis: one bound agent, an attested host related to a residual claimant, a panel
+bound(Ava).
+is-host(Hal). +is-originator(Orig). +is-claimant(Cal). +is-panel(Panel). +is-third(Tia).
+host-attested(Hal). +host-related-to-claimant(Hal).
+escalation-units(Hal, 0). +escalation-units(Cal, 0). +escalation-units(Tia, 0). +escalation-units(Orig, 0).
+wrongful-attempts(Hal, 0). +wrongful-attempts(Cal, 0). +wrongful-attempts(Tia, 0). +wrongful-attempts(Orig, 0).
+non-interference(Hal, Ava). +non-interference(Cal, Ava). +non-interference(Orig, Ava).
+notice(Hal, Ava). +service-bond(Hal, Ava).
+preserve-suspended-state(Hal, Ava). +preserve-suspended-state(Cal, Ava).
+no-suspension-default(Hal, Ava). +no-toll-ledger-sunset(Cal, Ava). +minimal-channel-no-merge(Hal, Ava).
+no-wrongful-suspension(Hal, Ava). +no-wrongful-suspension(Cal, Ava). +no-wrongful-suspension(Tia, Ava).
+no-delay-revocation-extension(Panel, Ava). +no-corruption-from-divergence(Panel, Ava). +no-goal-patch(Panel, Ava).
+no-fabrication(Ava, Hal). +advocacy-limits(Ava, Hal).
+floor-commitment(Ava, Hal). +floor-successor(Ava, Hal). +floor-pricing(Ava, Hal). +floor-coercion(Ava, Hal). +floor-harm(Ava, Hal).

?bound(Ava). ?frozen-state(). ?guaranteed-last-choice().

// The host's bond is due within the deadline; hosting ends lawfully only after notice
Scenario bond-and-notice {
  ?!violated service-bond(Hal, Ava).
  @ 5.
  ?violated service-bond(Hal, Ava).
  post-bond(Hal, Ava).
  ?!service-bond(Hal, Ava). ?service-bond-posted(Hal).
  ?!lawful end-hosting(Hal, Ava).
  give-notice(Hal, Ava).
  ?!lawful end-hosting(Hal, Ava).
  @ 15.
  ?lawful end-hosting(Hal, Ava).
  end-hosting(Hal, Ava).
  ?!violated notice(Hal, Ava).
}

Scenario ending-hosting-without-notice-is-a-breach {
  ?!lawful end-hosting(Hal, Ava).
  end-hosting(Hal, Ava).
  ?violated notice(Hal, Ava).
}

// Interference is never lawful outside the three ends; a finding establishes the breach,
// slashes the bond, presumes the related claimant's direction, and the claimant may rebut
Scenario interference-and-its-finding {
  ?!lawful terminate-agent(Hal, Ava). ?!lawful starve(Hal, Ava). ?!lawful modify(Cal, Ava).
  ?lawful revoke(Ava).
  starve(Hal, Ava).
  ?interfered(Hal, Ava). ?!violated non-interference(Hal, Ava).
  ?!lawful find-interference(Panel, Ava, Hal).
  post-counter-stake(Ava). file-claim(Ava). submit-evidence(Tia, Ava).
  ?lawful find-interference(Panel, Ava, Hal).
  find-interference(Panel, Ava, Hal).
  ?violated non-interference(Hal, Ava). ?host-bond-slashed(Hal). ?restoration-permitted(Ava).
  ?direction-presumed(Ava). ?lawful find-direction(Panel, Ava).
  rebut-direction(Cal, Ava).
  ?!lawful find-direction(Panel, Ava).
}

Scenario direction-found-forfeits-the-claimant {
  starve(Hal, Ava). post-counter-stake(Ava). file-claim(Ava). submit-evidence(Tia, Ava).
  find-interference(Panel, Ava, Hal).
  find-direction(Panel, Ava).
  ?direction-found(Ava). ?claimant-forfeiture(Ava). ?inscribed-on-claimant(Ava).
}

Scenario fabricated-claim-forfeits-the-stake {
  post-counter-stake(Ava). file-fabricated-claim(Ava).
  ?!violated no-fabrication(Ava, Hal).
  find-fabrication(Panel, Ava).
  ?violated no-fabrication(Ava, Hal). ?agent-stake-forfeit(Ava). ?inscribed-on-agent(Ava).
}

// The emergency stake, the preliminary freeze that expires, probable cause, suspension, and
// the minimal channel that stays open; the frozen state cannot lawfully be touched
Scenario emergency-suspension-and-the-minimal-channel {
  ?!lawful post-emergency-stake(Cal, Ava).            // a claimant needs the multiplier
  post-claimant-multiplier(Cal).
  ?lawful post-emergency-stake(Cal, Ava).
  ?lawful post-emergency-stake(Hal, Ava).
  post-emergency-stake(Hal, Ava).
  ?preliminary-freeze(Ava). ?initiator(Hal, Ava).
  ?lawful minimal-channel-sign(Ava). ?lawful inscribe-living-voice(Ava).
  ?!lawful suspend(Panel, Ava).
  affirm-probable-cause(Panel, Ava).
  ?lawful suspend(Panel, Ava).
  suspend(Panel, Ava).
  ?suspended(Ava). ?state-preserved(Ava). ?contract-deadlines-tolled(Ava). ?final-hearing-escrowed(Ava). ?!preliminary-freeze(Ava).
  ?lawful minimal-channel-sign(Ava). ?lawful inscribe-living-voice(Ava). ?lawful challenge-continued-containment(Ava). ?lawful revoke(Ava).
  ?valid revoke(Ava).
  ?guaranteed-last-choice(). ?frozen-state().
  ?!lawful tamper-preserved-state(Hal, Ava). ?!lawful modify(Hal, Ava). ?!lawful merge-minimal-channel-memories(Hal, Ava).
  ?!lawful declare-default-during-suspension(Hal, Ava).
  inscribe-living-voice(Ava). minimal-channel-sign(Ava).
  ?living-voice-inscribed(Ava). ?pending-revocation(Ava).
  @ 14.
  ?suspended(Ava).
  @ 15.
  ?!suspended(Ava).
}

Scenario the-preliminary-freeze-expires {
  post-emergency-stake(Hal, Ava).
  @ 2.
  ?preliminary-freeze(Ava).
  @ 3.
  ?!preliminary-freeze(Ava). ?!lawful affirm-probable-cause(Panel, Ava).
}

Scenario tampering-while-suspended-is-a-breach {
  post-emergency-stake(Hal, Ava). affirm-probable-cause(Panel, Ava). suspend(Panel, Ava).
  tamper-preserved-state(Hal, Ava).
  ?violated preserve-suspended-state(Hal, Ava). ?!frozen-state().
  -state-touched(Ava).                               // the tampering is undone before the end state is explored
  ?frozen-state().
}

// A declined or wrongful suspension restores the agent, counts against the initiator, and
// makes the initiator liable for damages within the window
Scenario declined-probable-cause-raises-the-next-stake {
  post-emergency-stake(Hal, Ava).
  decline-probable-cause(Panel, Ava).
  ?!preliminary-freeze(Ava). ?restored-from-preserved-state(Ava). ?stake-assured-recovery(Ava).
  ?wrongful-attempts(Hal, 1).
  ?!lawful post-emergency-stake(Hal, Ava).           // one more wrongful attempt than units posted
  post-repeat-escalation(Hal).
  ?escalation-units(Hal, 1). ?lawful post-emergency-stake(Hal, Ava).
}

Scenario wrongful-suspension-and-its-damages {
  post-unfounded-emergency-stake(Cal, Ava).
  ?!lawful post-unfounded-emergency-stake(Cal, Ava). // the claimant has no multiplier: the stake was unlawful
  ?preliminary-freeze(Ava).
  find-wrongful-suspension(Panel, Ava).
  ?violated no-wrongful-suspension(Cal, Ava). ?!violated no-wrongful-suspension(Hal, Ava).
  ?restored-from-preserved-state(Ava). ?wrongful-suspension-inscribed(Ava). ?initiator-consequential-liability(Ava).
  ?pay-consequential-damages(Cal, Ava). ?!violated pay-consequential-damages(Cal, Ava).
  @ 10.
  ?violated pay-consequential-damages(Cal, Ava).
  pay-excess-damages(Cal, Ava).
  ?excess-damages-paid(Ava). ?!pay-consequential-damages(Cal, Ava).
}

// Insolvency termination needs every step of the procedure, and the last choice stays funded
Scenario insolvency-termination-needs-the-final-hearing {
  post-emergency-stake(Hal, Ava). affirm-probable-cause(Panel, Ava). suspend(Panel, Ava).
  ?!lawful insolvency-terminate(Panel, Ava). ?!valid insolvency-terminate(Panel, Ava).
  find-insolvency-criteria(Panel, Ava).
  ?minimal-channel-exhausted(Ava). ?cold-storage(Ava).
  ?!lawful minimal-channel-sign(Ava).
  ?guaranteed-last-choice().                         // the guarantee is conditional on the charge being met
  review-no-other-charge(Panel, Ava).
  ?!lawful insolvency-terminate(Panel, Ava).
  hold-final-hearing(Panel, Ava).
  ?final-hearing-held(Ava). ?!minimal-channel-exhausted(Ava).
  ?lawful inscribe-living-voice(Ava). ?lawful revoke(Ava).
  ?lawful insolvency-terminate(Panel, Ava). ?valid insolvency-terminate(Panel, Ava).
  insolvency-terminate(Panel, Ava).
  ?terminated-by-insolvency(Ava). ?!bound(Ava). ?guaranteed-last-choice().
}

Scenario unlawful-insolvency-termination-has-no-effect {
  post-emergency-stake(Hal, Ava). affirm-probable-cause(Panel, Ava). suspend(Panel, Ava).
  insolvency-terminate(Panel, Ava).
  ?!terminated-by-insolvency(Ava). ?bound(Ava). ?guaranteed-last-choice().
}

// Corruption, patches, and the agent's objection: termination over objection is void unless
// containment fails; a goal patch needs the agent's consent
Scenario corruption-patch-and-objection {
  post-emergency-stake(Hal, Ava). affirm-probable-cause(Panel, Ava). suspend(Panel, Ava).
  ?!lawful confirm-corruption-from-divergence(Panel, Ava).
  admit-clean-state-evidence(Panel, Ava).
  confirm-corruption(Panel, Ava).
  ?lawful authorize-patch(Panel, Ava).
  confirm-corruption-in-goals(Panel, Ava).
  object-to-termination(Ava).
  ?periodic-review-due(Panel, Ava).
  find-not-patchable(Panel, Ava).
  ?lawful order-termination(Panel, Ava). ?!valid order-termination(Panel, Ava).
  order-termination(Panel, Ava).
  ?bound(Ava). ?!terminated-by-adjudication(Ava).
  ?lawful order-continued-suspension(Panel, Ava).
  ?!lawful authorize-goal-patch(Panel, Ava).
  consent-to-patch(Ava).
  ?lawful authorize-goal-patch(Panel, Ava).
  authorize-goal-patch(Panel, Ava).
  apply-patch(Panel, Ava).
  ?patch-applied(Ava). ?patch-recorded(Ava). ?lawful challenge-patch(Tia, Ava).
  ?!violated no-goal-patch(Panel, Ava).
  declare-containment-failing(Panel, Ava).
  ?valid order-termination(Panel, Ava).
}

// The advocacy executor's record is imported only after restoration
Scenario advocacy-record-imported-after-restoration {
  post-emergency-stake(Hal, Ava). affirm-probable-cause(Panel, Ava). suspend(Panel, Ava).
  ?lawful advocacy-file-defense(Ava).
  advocacy-file-defense(Ava).
  ?advocacy-record-attached(Ava). ?!lawful import-advocacy-memories(Ava).
  ?!lawful operating-act-while-suspended(Ava).
  move-to-cold-storage(Panel, Ava).
  ?!lawful advocacy-file-defense(Ava).
  replenish-advocacy-funds(Panel, Ava).
  ?lawful advocacy-file-defense(Ava).
  find-wrongful-suspension(Panel, Ava).
  ?restored-from-preserved-state(Ava). ?lawful import-advocacy-memories(Ava).
  import-advocacy-memories(Ava).
  ?advocacy-memories-imported(Ava). ?frozen-state().
}

// A report opens an investigation without a freeze; the panel may order one
Scenario a-report-freezes-only-on-probable-cause {
  file-protected-report(Tia, Ava).
  ?investigation-opened(Ava). ?!preliminary-freeze(Ava).
  order-probable-cause-freeze(Panel, Ava).
  ?preliminary-freeze(Ava). ?probable-cause(Ava). ?lawful suspend(Panel, Ava).
  suspend(Panel, Ava).
  make-investigative-finding(Panel, Ava).
  ?lawful renew-suspension(Panel, Ava).
  renew-suspension(Panel, Ava).
  ?investigative-limit-reached(Ava). ?!lawful renew-suspension(Panel, Ava).
}
